---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { firm } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { text: 'Acceptance of these terms', slug: 'acceptance-of-these-terms' },
  { text: 'No attorney-client relationship', slug: 'no-attorney-client-relationship' },
  { text: 'Information is not legal advice', slug: 'information-is-not-legal-advice' },
  { text: 'Communications and confidentiality', slug: 'communications-and-confidentiality' },
  { text: 'Deadlines and time-sensitive matters', slug: 'deadlines-and-time-sensitive-matters' },
  { text: 'Acceptable use', slug: 'acceptable-use' },
  { text: 'Intellectual property', slug: 'intellectual-property' },
  { text: 'Third-party links and resources', slug: 'third-party-links-and-resources' },
  { text: 'Disclaimer of warranties', slug: 'disclaimer-of-warranties' },
  { text: 'Limitation of liability', slug: 'limitation-of-liability' },
  { text: 'Indemnification', slug: 'indemnification' },
  { text: 'Governing law', slug: 'governing-law' },
  { text: 'Changes and severability', slug: 'changes-and-severability' },
  { text: 'Contact', slug: 'contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Sulfab Law Office P.C."
  description="The terms that govern use of the Sulfab Law Office P.C. website, including the limits of the information published and the rules for contacting the firm."
  h1="Terms of Service"
  eyebrow="Website Terms"
  lede="The rules that apply when you use this website, and the limits of the information published here."
  updated="2026-11-21"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service (“terms”) govern your use of the website at
    <a href="https://www.sulfablaw.com">sulfablaw.com</a>, operated by Sulfab Law Office P.C.
    (“the firm,” “we,” “us”). By using the website, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree,
    please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptance-of-these-terms">Acceptance of these terms</h2>
  <p>
    Your use of the website, including browsing, submitting a form, or calling a number listed here,
    is subject to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and
    <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>, which are incorporated by reference.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-attorney-client-relationship">No attorney-client relationship</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Contacting the firm through this website does not create an attorney-client relationship, and
      does not make the firm your lawyer.
    </strong>
    An attorney-client relationship begins only when the firm and the client sign a written
    engagement agreement and any required retainer is paid. Until then, the firm has not agreed to
    represent you, has not agreed to take any action on your behalf, and may represent another party
    whose interests are adverse to yours.
  </p>
  <p>
    We review inquiries for conflicts of interest before accepting a matter. Please do not assume a
    matter has been accepted because you submitted a form, left a voicemail, or received a reply
    acknowledging your message.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-is-not-legal-advice">Information is not legal advice</h2>
  <p>
    The articles, practice-area pages, service-area pages, FAQs, and other content on this website
    are general information for educational purposes. They are not legal advice, and they are not a
    substitute for a consultation with an attorney who has reviewed your facts. Immigration law
    changes frequently, and an answer that fits one person’s situation may be wrong for another.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reading this website does not make you a client, and relying on it instead of seeking advice can
    cause you to miss deadlines or lose options. If you have a pending case, a hearing date, or a
    notice from the government, speak with an attorney promptly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="communications-and-confidentiality">Communications and confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    Information you send before an engagement is not protected by the attorney-client privilege in
    the same way as information shared after the firm is retained. Please do not send confidential
    case documents, identification numbers, or sensitive personal records through the website’s
    general forms. If the firm agrees to review documents, we will tell you how to send them
    securely.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email and web-form messages can be delayed, misdirected, or intercepted. Sending a message does
    not guarantee that the firm has received it or that a deadline has been preserved.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deadlines-and-time-sensitive-matters">Deadlines and time-sensitive matters</h2>
  <p>
    Immigration matters often involve strict deadlines: the one-year asylum filing deadline,
    deadlines to appeal or move to reopen, bond and custody timelines, and court-ordered response
    dates. Nothing on this website extends a deadline. If you are in immigration detention or have a
    hearing or filing deadline approaching, call the firm directly at
    <a href={firm.phoneHref}>{firm.phoneDisplay}</a> rather than relying on a web form.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to use this website to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Violate any law or the rights of another person.</li>
    <li>Submit false, misleading, or impersonating information.</li>
    <li>Send spam, bulk solicitations, or automated queries.</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the site, its servers, or its data.</li>
    <li>Introduce malware or interfere with the site’s operation.</li>
    <li>Scrape, copy, or republish substantial portions of the content without permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="intellectual-property">Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design, graphics, layout, and other content on this website are owned by the firm or
    used under license and are protected by copyright and other laws. You may view, download, and
    print pages for your own personal, non-commercial use. Any other use — including reproduction,
    distribution, modification, or creation of derivative works — requires written permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    “Sulfab Law Office” and the firm’s emblem are identifiers of the firm and may not be used in a
    way that suggests endorsement or affiliation without permission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party-links-and-resources">Third-party links and resources</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to courts, government agencies, review profiles, map services, and other
    third-party sites. Those sites are not controlled by the firm, and we are not responsible for
    their content, accuracy, or privacy practices. A link is not an endorsement, and third-party
    information should be verified with the source.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimer-of-warranties">Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    This website and its content are provided “as is” and “as available.” To the fullest extent
    permitted by law, the firm disclaims all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of
    accuracy, completeness, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
    non-infringement. We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of
    harmful components, or that the information is current as of the moment you read it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="limitation-of-liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, the firm and its attorneys and staff will not be liable
    for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use
    of, or inability to use, this website or its content. This includes lost opportunities, missed
    deadlines, or reliance on information published here. Nothing in these terms limits liability
    that cannot be limited under applicable law or the rules of professional conduct.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnification">Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold harmless the firm and its attorneys and staff from claims,
    losses, or expenses, including reasonable attorneys’ fees, arising from your violation of these
    terms or your misuse of the website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to conflict of
    law principles. Any dispute relating to the website or these terms will be brought in the state
    or federal courts located in San Francisco County, California, and you consent to their
    jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes-and-severability">Changes and severability</h2>
  <p>
    We may revise these terms at any time by posting an updated version on this page. The “last
    updated” date shows the current version. Continued use of the website after a change means you
    accept the revised terms. If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay
    in effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sulfab Law Office P.C.</strong></li>
    <li>{firm.address.street}, {firm.address.city}, {firm.address.state} {firm.address.zip}</li>
    <li>Email: <a href={firm.emailHref}>{firm.email}</a></li>
    <li>Telephone: <a href={firm.phoneHref}>{firm.phoneDisplay}</a></li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
